"1173-1181","abstractText":"Adenylyl cyclases (ACs) are a group of widely distributed enzymes whose functions are very diverse. There are nine known transmembrane AC isoforms activated by Gαs. Each has its own pattern of expression in the digestive system and differential regulation of function by Ca(2+) and other intracellular signals. In addition to the transmembrane isoforms, one AC is soluble and exhibits distinct regulation. In this review, the basic structure, regulation and physiological roles of ACs in the digestive system are discussed.","affiliation":"Department of Biological Sciences, Georgia Regents University, United States. Electronic address: msabbatini@gru.edu.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Review","Journal Article","Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"grantId":"R01 DK054021","agency":"NIDDK NIH HHS","acronym":"DK","orderIn":0},{"agency":"VA Career Development and Merit Awards","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"R01DK54021","agency":"NIDDK NIH HHS","acronym":"DK","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"DK54021","agency":"NIH R01","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"I01 BX000929","agency":"BLRD VA","acronym":"BX","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Digestive System","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"EN","qualifierName":"enzymology","majorTopic_YN":"Y"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Pancreatitis","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"EN","qualifierName":"enzymology","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Isoenzymes","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"PH","qualifierName":"physiology","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Signal Transduction"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Catalytic Domain"},{"ma